# ReviewEase (Review Assistant)

QR flow that phrases a diner's own experience, then hands them to Google. Owners get private feedback. We are a review assistant, not a review generator.

## Stack

- `/apps/web` — Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind + Framer Motion, PWA. Host: Vercel.
- `/apps/api` — FastAPI + Pydantic + SQLAlchemy + Alembic. Host: Render/Fly/Railway.
- Postgres (Supabase or Neon). Auth for owner/admin only (Supabase Auth or JWT). Diners are anonymous.
- LLM chain: Groq (Llama 3.1 8B Instant) → Gemini Flash-Lite → template fallback. Model names in env.

```
apps/web/app/r/[slug]/page.tsx
apps/web/components/steps/{Dishes,Ratings,Tags,FreeText,Tone,Draft,Done}.tsx
apps/web/components/ui/{ProgressBar,EmojiRating,TagChip,DishCard}.tsx
apps/web/lib/{api,clipboard}.ts
apps/web/app/dashboard/*
apps/api/   # routes, models, llm gateway, alembic
```

QR encodes `https://app.com/r/{slug}?t={table}` only. Open Google via `https://search.google.com/local/writereview?placeid=` after the diner copies the draft.

## Coding

- Type every boundary: TypeScript on the web, Pydantic models on the API. No untyped payloads.
- Keep modules small: one step, provider, or check per file.
- No secrets, API keys, or password hashes in source. Config comes from env; document keys in `.env.example` only (`DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `ALLOWED_ORIGIN`, `LLM_CHAIN`, `GROQ_*`, `GEMINI_*`).

```python
# BAD: groq_key = "gsk_live_..."
# GOOD: groq_key = os.environ["GROQ_API_KEY"]
```

## Product

- Drafts use ONLY customer-provided facts (dishes, ratings, tags, free text). Never invent dishes, prices, staff, events, or praise.
- No auto-posting to Google. The diner taps Submit on Google themselves.
- No rewards, discounts, or points tied to posting a review. Participation badges may exist later; they must not depend on a Google post.
- No review gating. Private feedback and the Google handoff are available at every rating.
